Fixes for checkConsistentColls.

checkConsistentColls was supposed to be checking that two collections are
the same, but it was really only checking that the sizes of the collections
are the same.

It goes through one collection and does a binary_search for the item
in the other collection.  But first, the result of the binary_search
was ignored, and second, the collections are documented as being unordered,
so binary_search isn't appropriate in any case.

Rewrite to try to fix this.  To avoid N^2 behavior, copy the collection
that's a simple vector<string>, normalize the names, and sort it.
We can then binary_search within that vector.

Fixes warnings seen with gcc16.
